IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`
IMPORT `cda-s4-punishment`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, section 4: TESTS.
-- Layer 1 tests. Every expected value below was written from the text before the
-- file was run. A failing assertion here would be a finding, not a value to be edited.

§ `Tests for section 4`

§§ `4(1): arson under section 1, and any offence under section 1(2)`

-- s 4(1): an offence under section 1(1), not by fire. Expected: life does not apply (section 1(1) other than arson is not named in s 4(1)).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`)

-- s 4(1): arson under section 1(1). Expected: life applies ('arson under section 1').
#ASSERT `section 4(1) applies to` `arson under section 1(1)`

-- s 4(1): an offence under section 1(2), not by fire. Expected: life applies ('an offence under section 1(2) (whether arson or not)').
#ASSERT `section 4(1) applies to` `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire`

-- s 4(1): arson under section 1(2). Expected: life applies (arson, and an offence under 1(2)).
#ASSERT `section 4(1) applies to` `arson under section 1(2)`

-- s 4(1): an offence under section 2(a). Expected: life does not apply (s 4(1) does not name section 2).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` `an offence under section 2(a)`)

-- s 4(1): an offence under section 2(b). Expected: life does not apply (s 4(1) does not name section 2).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` `an offence under section 2(b)`)

-- s 4(1): an offence under section 3(a). Expected: life does not apply (s 4(1) does not name section 3).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` `an offence under section 3(a)`)

-- s 4(1): an offence under section 3(b). Expected: life does not apply (s 4(1) does not name section 3).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(1) applies to` `an offence under section 3(b)`)

§§ `4(2): any other offence`

-- s 4(2): an offence under section 1(1), not by fire. Expected: ten years applies (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT `section 4(2) applies to` `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`

-- s 4(2): arson under section 1(1). Expected: ten years does not apply (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(2) applies to` `arson under section 1(1)`)

-- s 4(2): an offence under section 1(2), not by fire. Expected: ten years does not apply (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(2) applies to` `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire`)

-- s 4(2): arson under section 1(2). Expected: ten years does not apply (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT NOT (`section 4(2) applies to` `arson under section 1(2)`)

-- s 4(2): an offence under section 2(a). Expected: ten years applies (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT `section 4(2) applies to` `an offence under section 2(a)`

-- s 4(2): an offence under section 2(b). Expected: ten years applies (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT `section 4(2) applies to` `an offence under section 2(b)`

-- s 4(2): an offence under section 3(a). Expected: ten years applies (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT `section 4(2) applies to` `an offence under section 3(a)`

-- s 4(2): an offence under section 3(b). Expected: ten years applies (exactly the offences s 4(1) does not name).
#ASSERT `section 4(2) applies to` `an offence under section 3(b)`

-- s 4(2): the ceiling is ten years. Expected: 10.
#ASSERT `the ceiling in years in section 4(2)` EQUALS 10

§§ `The most that can follow, on conviction on indictment`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 1(1), not by fire']. Expected: ten years (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['arson under section 1(1)']. Expected: life (s 4(1)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `arson under section 1(1)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 1(2), not by fire']. Expected: life (s 4(1)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire`) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['arson under section 1(2)']. Expected: life (s 4(1)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `arson under section 1(2)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 2(a)']. Expected: ten years (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 2(a)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 2(b)']. Expected: ten years (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 2(b)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 3(a)']. Expected: ten years (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 3(a)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 3(b)']. Expected: ten years (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 3(b)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 1(1), not by fire', 'an offence under section 3(a)']. Expected: ten years (two offences, neither named in s 4(1): ten years).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`, `an offence under section 3(a)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 1(1), not by fire', 'an offence under section 1(2), not by fire']. Expected: life (the 1(2) offence carries life; the heavier ceiling is the answer).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`, `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire`) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 2(a)', 'arson under section 1(1)']. Expected: life (arson in the list: life).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 2(a)`, `arson under section 1(1)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['arson under section 1(1)', 'arson under section 1(2)']. Expected: life (two arsons: life).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `arson under section 1(1)`, `arson under section 1(2)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

-- s 4: on indictment, offences ['an offence under section 3(b)', 'an offence under section 2(b)', 'an offence under section 1(1), not by fire']. Expected: ten years (three offences, none named in s 4(1): ten years).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` (LIST `an offence under section 3(b)`, `an offence under section 2(b)`, `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term not exceeding` 10

-- s 4: no offence committed, on indictment. Expected: no penalty (nothing to punish).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on conviction on indictment` EMPTY EQUALS `no offence under this Act, so no penalty`

§§ `The most that can follow, on summary conviction`

-- s 4 is silent about summary conviction (arson). Expected: the explicit not-stated value, not a number.
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on summary conviction` (LIST `arson under section 1(1)`) EQUALS `no maximum is stated in this text for that mode of conviction`

-- s 4 is silent about summary conviction (section 3(a)). Expected: the explicit not-stated value.
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on summary conviction` (LIST `an offence under section 3(a)`) EQUALS `no maximum is stated in this text for that mode of conviction`

-- s 4, summary conviction, no offence committed. Expected: no penalty (nothing to punish).
#ASSERT `the most that can follow` `on summary conviction` EMPTY EQUALS `no offence under this Act, so no penalty`
